heptapod@gmail.com wrote:
>
> I know if someone could not normally become proficient with a weapon,
> they are granted access to the appropriate skill should their deity
> deign to donate an antique endowment upon a favored soul.

Gifts from your deity - With weapons the skill slot gets unlocked.  With
a spellbook it comes blessed so you are guaranteed to be able to read
it.

> If someone doesn't normally have access to the long sword skill dips a
> long sword and gets Excalibur is the skill unlocked?

The principle applies - The lady of the fountain is not a deity so she
can make the sword very nice but she can't bless you.  If you get an
artifact by wishing, purchase, find it on the floor, kill a monster
carrying it, etc none of those methods open up the slot either.

But with Excalibur the news is good.  If you can get it from dipping you
are lawful.  It is the crowning gift for lawfuls.  When you get crowned
as a lawful your long sword skill slot is opened whether you already
have Excalibur or you get it then, plus other skill slots might get
opened depending on the situation.


